{"contents":[{"uri":"montagent://schema/def/Ease.json","mimeType":"application/json","text":"{
  "anyOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "montagent://schema/def/EaseName.json"
    },
    {
      "type": "array",
      "prefixItems": [
        {
          "type": "number",
          "format": "double",
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "maximum": 1.0,
          "description": "`x1` — the curve's own time, which runs from 0 to 1. Outside that is a schema error (ADR-0012)."
        },
        {
          "type": "number",
          "format": "double",
          "description": "`y1` — outside `[0, 1]` is legal, because overshoot is a real need beziers give away free (ADR-0012)."
        },
        {
          "type": "number",
          "format": "double",
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "maximum": 1.0,
          "description": "`x2` — the curve's own time, which runs from 0 to 1. Outside that is a schema error (ADR-0012)."
        },
        {
          "type": "number",
          "format": "double",
          "description": "`y2` — outside `[0, 1]` is legal, because overshoot is a real need beziers give away free (ADR-0012)."
        }
      ],
      "items": {
        "type": "number",
        "format": "double"
      },
      "minItems": 4,
      "maxItems": 4,
      "description": "`[x1, y1, x2, y2]`. `x` outside `[0,1]` is a schema error; `y` outside is legal,\nbecause overshoot is a real need beziers give away free."
    }
  ],
  "description": "The closed easing set: a published name, or the four control points directly.\n\nADR-0012: *\"A name is sugar over one evaluator, never a second mechanism.\"* The raw\nform is forced rather than chosen — splitting `ease-in-out` at an arbitrary instant\nyields a bezier that is no named ease and is not in the family, and snapping to the\nnearest name costs more framing than the reading `shift` was disqualified for."
}
"}]}

